a real: median over robots of the realised steering coefficient read back from the runtime weights
(signed path sum to depth 4, motif.py's quantity; the sign is the published motif's frame, so it is
negative on a forward-driving population by construction).  |a|/|c|: gradient over common mode, same
readback.  delta: paired change in items against the robot's own baseline on the same seeds, mean
over the 7 robots, CI bootstrapped over robots (20000 draws); se/bout is the naive per-bout standard
error for comparison only.  zero d: paired differences that are exactly 0; zero i: bouts with no items.
in-disc m: path length while the centre of mass is inside the food disc; items/m: items per in-disc
metre (mean over robots of each robot's ratio).  rail%: control ticks with both drive effectors pinned
beyond |0.99| with the same sign -- pure steering, zero throttle.  expl: bouts that exploded.

